'' SEEK, COLOR AND A WIDE WRITE ITEM -- three statement kinds that reached the
'' dispatcher and fell off the end of it. Every RTL entry point they need was already
'' declared in rtl.bi; what was missing was the lowering.
''
'' COLOR's THIRD ARGUMENT IS A MASK OF WHAT WAS OMITTED, and that is not derivable
'' from the argument count -- measured, all four spellings:
''
''   color 1, 2   fb_Color( 1, 2, 0u )      color 3   fb_Color( 3, 0, 2u )
''   color , 4    fb_Color( 0, 4, 1u )      color     fb_Color( 0, 0, 3u )
''
'' -- so bit 1 says the FOREGROUND was not written and bit 2 the BACKGROUND, and an
'' omitted argument passes 0. Reading it as a COUNT would answer correctly for two of
'' the four.
''
'' WRITE's wide item asked LowerAddr for an address, which only an addressable wide
'' VARIABLE has, so 'write #1, wstr( "W" )' had nothing to pass and the whole statement
'' declined. WideOperand_ knows all three spellings and is what every other wide site
'' already asks. file/encod.bas is three of them.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/seek-color-write.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_FileSeekLarge
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WriteWstr
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_Color(0, 0, 3)
'' GOLDEN: expected/seek-color-write.out
